# Mission Control - environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in, or just export the vars in your shell.
# EVERYTHING BELOW IS OPTIONAL. With no keys at all the whole system still
# runs: brain.sv.jac falls back to byLLM's MockLLM and the UI badge reads
# "MOCK" instead of "LIVE".
#
# Provider precedence at import time: GROQ_API_KEY -> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> mock.
# byLLM reads these directly; do NOT put a key in jac.toml, and never commit .env.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groq (preferred — very low latency, ideal for the per-tick sim loop)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this and the Incident Commander + Rescue Team reason against
# groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile. brain_mode() then reports "live".
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic (fallback if no Groq key — uses claude-sonnet-4-6)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override the project default model for one shell (byLLM built-in), e.g.:
# BYLLM_DEFAULT_MODEL=groq/llama-3.3-70b-versatile
